From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:57:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ether: tell the modem Wi-Fi calling is provisioned, and let
 the ACDB paths be set

Wi-Fi calling has never got past the modem declining it. Toggling WFC does reach the modem and the
QMI transaction succeeds, and the modem answers:

    client_provisioning_config_ind_hdlr: .. client_prov_enabled: 0
                                         .. wifi_call_preference: 0    (1 was sent)

It is not failing, it is declining: we have been setting the user's preference for a feature it does
not consider provisioned. Of the seven client-provisioning items the RIL exposes we send WIFI_CALL
and WIFI_CALL_PREFERENCE, and never ENABLE_VOWIFI.

The reason is in ImsManager.isWfcProvisionedOnDevice(): it only reaches the branch that pushes the
provisioning value when isMmTelProvisioningRequired(VOICE, IWLAN) is true. Ours was false, so it
short-circuited to "provisioned" locally and sent nothing. That also explains why VoLTE is
unaffected: VoLTE works because the modem's own carrier config enables it, so it never needed this
path. Wi-Fi calling, which that config does not enable, is exactly the feature that does.

ims.mmtel_requires_provisioning_bundle turns it on for VOICE over IWLAN alone. The deprecated global
carrier_volte_provisioning_required_bool stays false deliberately: switching that on would gate
working VoLTE on provisioning as well, which is a bad trade for a feature that has never worked. The
int array holds registration techs, and listing only 1 (IWLAN) leaves VoLTE falling through to the
old key, ungated.

Traced the whole chain rather than assuming it: the value goes out as
ProvisioningManager.KEY_VOICE_OVER_WIFI_ENABLED_OVERRIDE, which is 28, the same number as legacy 7.1
ImsConfig VOICE_OVER_WIFI_SETTING_ENABLED, so the bridge forwards it unchanged and QCRIL maps it to
CLIENT_PROVISIONING_ENABLE_VOWIFI.

Separately, from a sweep of property *set* denials, which name the property where read denials do
not: vendor_init is refused audio_prop, so the seven persist.audio.calfile* paths init.qcom.rc sets
from this device's own ACDB data all read back empty and the audio HAL has been on generic
calibration since the port began. AOSP folded the exported_audio_prop type vendor_init used to hold
back into audio_prop; vendor rc files written against the old world stopped working silently.
---
 .../apps/CarrierConfig/res/xml/vendor.xml     | 28 +++++++++++++++++++
 sepolicy/vendor_init.te                       | 11 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 39 insertions(+)

diff --git a/overlay/packages/apps/CarrierConfig/res/xml/vendor.xml b/overlay/packages/apps/CarrierConfig/res/xml/vendor.xml
index cc1f91b..dd7b8f7 100644
--- a/overlay/packages/apps/CarrierConfig/res/xml/vendor.xml
+++ b/overlay/packages/apps/CarrierConfig/res/xml/vendor.xml
@@ -20,5 +20,33 @@
         <boolean name="carrier_volte_override_wfc_provisioning_bool" value="true" />
         <int name="carrier_default_wfc_ims_mode_int" value="1" />
         <int name="carrier_default_wfc_ims_roaming_mode_int" value="1" />
+
+        <!-- Require IMS provisioning for VOICE over IWLAN, and only that.
+
+             Without this the modem is never told Wi-Fi calling is provisioned, and answers every
+             attempt to configure it by declining:
+
+                 client_provisioning_config_ind_hdlr: client_prov_enabled: 0
+                                                      wifi_call_preference: 0   (1 was sent)
+
+             ImsManager.isWfcProvisionedOnDevice() only reaches the branch that pushes the
+             provisioning value when isMmTelProvisioningRequired(VOICE, IWLAN) is true; otherwise it
+             short-circuits to "provisioned" locally and nothing is sent. So Android has been setting
+             the user's WFC *preference* on a feature the modem considers unprovisioned.
+
+             That then reaches the modem as ProvisioningManager.KEY_VOICE_OVER_WIFI_ENABLED_OVERRIDE,
+             which is 28: the same number as legacy 7.1 ImsConfig VOICE_OVER_WIFI_SETTING_ENABLED,
+             so the bridge forwards it unchanged and QCRIL maps it to CLIENT_PROVISIONING_ENABLE_VOWIFI.
+
+             Per-capability and per-tech deliberately. The deprecated
+             carrier_volte_provisioning_required_bool above stays false: it is global, and turning it
+             on would gate working VoLTE on provisioning too. The array holds registration techs
+             (ImsRegistrationImplBase): 0 LTE, 1 IWLAN, 2 CROSS_SIM, 3 NR. Only IWLAN is listed, so
+             VoLTE keeps falling through to the deprecated key and stays ungated. -->
+        <pbundle_as_map name="ims.mmtel_requires_provisioning_bundle">
+            <int-array name="ims.capability_type_voice_int_array" num="1">
+                <item value="1" />
+            </int-array>
+        </pbundle_as_map>
     </carrier_config>
 </carrier_config_list>
diff --git a/sepolicy/vendor_init.te b/sepolicy/vendor_init.te
index 57d9d14..ec22c3b 100644
--- a/sepolicy/vendor_init.te
+++ b/sepolicy/vendor_init.te
@@ -15,3 +15,14 @@ allow vendor_init radio_data_file:file create_file_perms;
 
 # copy_complete under the radio core data dir
 allow vendor_init radio_core_data_file:file create_file_perms;
+
+# init.qcom.rc sets persist.audio.calfile0..6 to this device's own ACDB calibration
+# (NBQ_Speaker_cal.acdb, NBQ_Handset_cal.acdb, NBQ_Headset_cal.acdb and four more) and every one is
+# refused, so all seven read back empty and the audio HAL has been running on generic calibration:
+#   avc: denied { set } for property=persist.audio.calfile0 scontext=u:r:vendor_init:s0
+#                                                           tcontext=u:object_r:audio_prop:s0
+# AOSP used to grant vendor_init the separate exported_audio_prop type and folded it back into
+# audio_prop, which silently broke vendor rc files written against the old world. public/vendor_init.te
+# already grants vendor_init a long list of other core property types, and there is no neverallow
+# against this one.
+set_prop(vendor_init, audio_prop)
